The user wants a JSON response estimating software development effort based on a provided specification.
The specification describes a Spring Framework-based project with 8 user stories (U1-U8).
I need to:
1. Break down the development into activities.
2. State technical/design decisions and assumptions.
3. Provide a most likely effort estimate (in work-hours) for each activity.
4. Calculate the total effort.
5. Return ONLY valid JSON matching the provided schema.

User Stories Analysis:
U1: Documentation for custom module standards/patterns. (Docs)
U2: Host custom module (uber-jar) in HDFS for deployment. (Deployment/Infra)
U3: Native WebSocket sink for full-duplex comms. (Feature dev)
U4: Research CI options (npm-cache) to improve stability. (CI/Research)
U5: EC2 CI infrastructure improvements (distributed jvm test, gradlew, embedded hadoop off, maxParallelForks). (CI/DevOps)
U6: Investigate WARN logs, fix PMD/Sonar violations, notify committer via Sonar. (Code quality/CI)
U7: Setup CI infrastructure for Windows OS (Bamboo, powershell, redis, rabbit, etc.). (CI/DevOps)
U8: Common shared location for dependent jars (xd/lib folder, classloader workaround). (Infra/Config)

Activities Breakdown:
A1: Documentation for Custom Module (U1)
A2: HDFS Hosting for Custom Module (U2)
A3: Native WebSocket Sink Implementation (U3)
A4: CI Options Research and npm-cache Integration (U4)
A5: EC2 CI Infrastructure Improvements (U5)
A6: Log Investigation and Sonar/PMD Violation Fixes (U6)
A7: Windows OS CI Infrastructure Setup (U7)
A8: Shared Dependency Location Configuration (U8)

